.SH "نام (NAME)"
postfix2dlf_main \- convert postfix2dlf_pre output to email dlf
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBpostfix2dlf_main\fR \fIdumpfile\fR
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBpostfix2dlf_main\fR expect a preprocessed postfix logfile, as written by
\&\fBpostfix2dlf_pre\fR\|(1) on STDIN.  It prints a Lire email DLF file on stdout, using
a Berkeley DB in \fIdumpfile\fR, holding a mapping from hostname\-queueid to
number\-of\-lines\-with\-this\-id.
.SH DEVELOPERS
.IX Header "DEVELOPERS"
Datastructures are the same as the ones in sendmail2dlf.
.PP
\&\f(CW%msg\fR stores all currently being processed information from the log.  In
sendmail2dlf, this hash is indexed by dlfid\*(Aqs:
.PP
.Vb 1
\& $dlfid = $log\->{\*(Aqhostname\*(Aq} . $log\->{\*(Aqqueueid\*(Aq}
.Ve
.PP
\&.  In postfix2dlf we use just the queueid, for now.
.PP
Scalar values:
.PP
.Vb 12
\& $msg{$dlfid} = {
\&   logrelay        => ...,
\&   queueid         => ...,
\&   time            => ...,
\&   nrcpts          => ...,
\&   from_user       => ...,
\&   from_domain     => ...,
\&   from_relay_host => ...,
\&   from_relay_ip   => ...,
\&   size            => ...,
\&   msgid           => ...,
\& };
.Ve
.PP
Furthermore:
.PP
.Vb 1
\& $del = $msg{$dlfid}\->{deliveries}{$to};
.Ve
.PP
\&\f(CW$to\fR is an email address as returned by &Lire::Email::sanitize_tos .
.PP
.Vb 2
\& $del\->{to_user}   = ....;
\& $del\->{to_domain} = ....;
.Ve
.PP
Other \f(CW$del\fR keys with scalar values:
.PP
.Vb 6
\& to_relay_host
\& to_relay_ip
\& delay
\& xdelay
\& stat
\& xstat
.Ve
.PP
\&.
.PP
The hash reference \f(CW$msg\fR{$dlfid} is often assigned to \`$cur\*(Aq.
.SH "مثال‌ها (EXAMPLES)"
.IX Header "EXAMPLES"
postfix2dlf_main will be rarely used on its own: it is called by
\&\fBpostfix2dlf\fR\|(1).  Refer to the postfix2dlf manpage for examples and usage
information.
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBpostfix2dlf\fR\|(1), \fBpostfix2dlf_pre\fR\|(1), \fBsendmail2dlf\fR\|(1)
